Even if in general "your internet is (or feels) plenty fast", that's
probably download speeds and such you're thinking of. But when playing
NetHack on a server, it's not the throughput that counts, it's the response
times, since there is not much data to be transmitted at once, but there is
some data to be transmitted every time you press a button. Using "ping"
will give you an estimate on how long it takes for a data packet to get to
a given server and back.

The connection hardware at your site is mostly irrelevant to this, it's the
whole route from you to the NAO server. Not much you can do about that,
except find another NH server that gives you lower pings.

